s emitted unchanged, because escaping cannot protect such a delimiter\n- **AND** the documented guarantee does not claim otherwise\n\n#### Scenario: Single-line value cannot escape its label\n\n- **WHEN** a value projected for single-line use contains line breaks\n- **THEN** the line breaks are removed before rendering\n- **AND** the value cannot continue past the label's line\n\n\"\"\"\nt = t.replace(old_e, new_e, 1)\nIC.write_text(t); print(\"instance-config rewritten\")\n\n# --- model-system-prompts: keep the summary consistent ---\nMS = pathlib.Path(\"openspec/changes/adopt-handlebars-prompt-templates/specs/model-system-prompts/spec.md\")\nm = MS.read_text()\nm = m.replace(\n\"Rendered values SHALL be escaped only for characters that could forge a structural delimiter, leaving prose punctuation intact, and SHALL be escaped when the context is built rather than by mutating the engine's global escaping.\",\n\"Rendered values SHALL be escaped by replacing exactly `&`, `<`, and `>`, leaving all other punctuation verbatim, and SHALL be escaped when the context is built rather than by mutating the engine's global escaping. The resulting guarantee is narrow and MUST NOT be overstated: delimiter integrity holds only for delimiters composed of those characters, and values projected for single-line use SHALL have line breaks removed.\", 1)\nm = m.replace(\n\"Referencing a context path outside the allowlist, emitting unescaped output, referencing a partial, invoking any other helper, or leaving a stale pre-cutover `${...}` expression SHALL fail startup naming the model id and the offending construct without printing prompt contents.\",\n\"Validation SHALL permit only an allowlisted set of node kinds — literal content, value expressions, block expressions, and comments — rejecting everything else by default, including partials in any form (plain, with a fallback block, or defined through a decorator). Referencing a context path outside the allowlist, emitting unescaped output, invoking any helper other than `if`/`unless`, using inverse-section shorthand, or leaving a stale pre-cutover legacy expression SHALL fail startup naming the model id and the offending construct without printing prompt contents.\", 1)\nMS.write_text(m); print(\"model-system-prompts updated\")\nPY\npnpm exec prettier --write 'openspec/changes/adopt-handlebars-prompt-templates/**/*.md' >/dev/null 2>&1\nopenspec validate adopt-handlebars-prompt-templates 2>&1 | tail -2",
